## Environment Variables

Every provider attribute can also be provided via an environment variable:

| Attribute  | Environment variable | Description                                                    |
|------------|----------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| `url`      | `INFLUXDB_URL`       | The InfluxDB server URL. Trailing slashes are ignored.         |
| `token`    | `INFLUXDB_TOKEN`     | An InfluxDB API token.                                         |
| `username` | `INFLUXDB_USERNAME`  | The InfluxDB username (used together with `password`).         |
| `password` | `INFLUXDB_PASSWORD`  | The InfluxDB password (used together with `username`).         |

Values set in the provider configuration take precedence over environment variables.

### Example

#### Token-based authentication

```terraform
export INFLUXDB_URL="http://localhost:8086"
export INFLUXDB_TOKEN="influxdb-token"

provider "influxdb" {}

terraform plan
```

#### Username and password authentication

```terraform
export INFLUXDB_URL="http://localhost:8086"
export INFLUXDB_USERNAME="influxdb-user"
export INFLUXDB_PASSWORD="influxdb-password"

provider "influxdb" {}

terraform plan
```

## Debugging

Setting [`TF_LOG=DEBUG`](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/internals/debugging) (or `TF_LOG_PROVIDER=DEBUG`) makes the provider log every HTTP request and response it exchanges with the InfluxDB API, including URLs, headers, and bodies:

```shell
export TF_LOG=DEBUG
terraform plan
```

Credentials are never written to these logs:

* The `Authorization` header is injected below the logging layer, so it does not appear in logged request headers.
* Configured tokens and passwords are masked (replaced with `***`) wherever they would otherwise appear, including sign-in headers, session cookies, and response bodies.

